# P2-AR-0014 re-run of delta-r.DERIVED-VIEWS-JKLMN (unedited) at worktree HEAD 473c3fba12a64cc36144c192c02b07f5db63fa04 dirty=1; gov sha256 bd1106a51a0d89efca2ebd734c880510cb35795d53a092e2592df7d37dc6fa81; 2026-09-18T23:58:41Z
---- owner-source universe (family delta) ----
J1 (line 596) Research becomes evidence: 8 bullets -> L598: question/reason; L599: method; L600: sources/data; L601: measurements; L602: uncertainty; L603: conclusion; L604: confidence; L605: influenced decisions/tasks
J2 (line 607) Experiment lifecycle: 7 bullets -> L608: hypothesis/question; L609: method/data; L610: reproducibility; L611: results; L612: interpretation; L613: decision influence; L614: production merge prohibited where experimental
K1 (line 622) CIT-P: 4 bullets -> L623: Proposed material change triggers deterministic graph traversal.; L624: Semantic/lexical/code candidates can supplement impact.; L625: Impact radius is produced.; L626: Human-readable consequences are surfaced.
K2 (line 628) CIT-E: 8 bullets -> L629: Final decision; L630: mutation manifest; L631: authoritative updates; L632: staleness/retest/rework propagation; L633: derived-view regeneration; L634: memory/index refresh; L635: verification; L636: commit or rollback/block atomically
K3 (line 638) Automatic impact simulation: 8 bullets -> L640: architecture; L641: behaviour; L642: interfaces; L643: security; L644: governance/policy; L645: infrastructure cost; L646: acceptance criteria; L647: data migration
K4 (line 649) Impact radius: 1 bullets -> L650: R0-R5 or equivalent affects traversal/test scope/model tier/agents/human approval/rollback.
L1 (line 656) Contradiction resolution: 4 bullets -> L657: deterministic precedence first; L658: low-impact/reversible/high-confidence agent resolution where allowed; L659: human escalation for consequential uncertainty; L660: rationale/evidence recorded
L2 (line 662) Human Decision Gate package: 10 bullets -> L663: plain-language question; L664: why now; L665: current state; L666: options; L667: impact; L668: reversibility; L669: cost/rework; L670: recommendation; L671: confidence; L672: exact permitted next actions
L3 (line 674) Gate presentation: 5 bullets -> L675: Gate in a file only is NOT presented.; L676: It must surface in active human interface.; L677: Presented ≠ answered.; L678: Declined/revoked/stale/other-CIT gates cannot authorise execution.; L679: Human approval cannot be fabricated by agent/CLI metadata.
L4 (line 681) Non-global blocking: 2 bullets -> L682: Independent runnable branches continue.; L683: Global stop only when policy or critical-path state requires.
M1 (line 689) T0-T3 or equivalent capability tiers: 4 bullets -> L690: deterministic/no-LLM route; L691: lightweight route; L692: strong engineering route; L693: frontier/high-reasoning route
M2 (line 695) Reasoning requirement: 1 bullets -> L696: low/medium/high/extra-high or equivalent minimum can be declared/enforced.
M3 (line 698) Role defaults: 2 bullets -> L699: orchestration/memory/audit default to strong enough tier.; L700: provider names are mapped externally without rewriting project state.
M4 (line 702) Empirical routing: 8 bullets -> L704: model/provider; L705: task class; L706: reasoning effort; L707: cost; L708: latency; L709: pass/fail; L710: repair count; L711: reviewer findings
N1 (line 717) Structured checkpoint: 9 bullets -> L719: session/role/task/mode/claim; L720: last completed step; L721: next action; L722: pending decisions/questions; L723: open transactions; L724: files changed; L725: test status; L726: context packet hash; L727: memory snapshot/state reference
N2 (line 729) Mandatory triggers: 8 bullets -> L730: task transition; L731: material decision; L732: accepted CIT; L733: significant mutation; L734: before handoff; L735: before model/provider switch; L736: before session close; L737: before known compaction
N3 (line 739) Provider-independent checkpoint watchdog: 3 bullets -> L740: Does not depend solely on proprietary hooks.; L741: Can mark checkpoint stale when material state changed.; L742: Handoff/session close can be blocked or degraded when checkpoint freshness violates policy.
N4 (line 744) Worker return contract: 1 bullets -> L745: structured result survives subagent conversation death.
